{
  "id": "043",
  "title": "Day One Stat Screen",
  "subtitle": "\"The infection landed at 6:42 AM. The stat screen appeared at 6:44. I had two minutes to read it before the first zombie reached my building.\"",
  "penName": "Remi Ash",
  "genre": "apocalypseZombie",
  "hook": "I was a single mother in Denver. My son Noah was six. At 6:42 on a Tuesday in June, a pale-blue stat screen appeared in my field of vision and told me I had been awakened. Two minutes later I heard the first screams. The infection moved at fifteen miles per hour. I had a Honda Civic, four bottles of water, a can opener, Noah's stuffed rabbit, and a Class: Fieldworker, Rank F. We were on I-70 headed west by 7:03. By sunset, we were not alone.",
